#
# NoCloud network-config (cloud-init "Networking Config Version 2" / netplan v2).
#
# This is the third file of the NoCloud seed, beside user-data and meta-data, and it is the one a
# from-scratch bootstrap cannot omit. A pristine cloud image relies on cloud-init to bring the
# network up; a fresh `import_raw_vdi` disk has no persisted network state, so without this file the
# VM boots to a login prompt with no DHCP, no address, and no agent that can reach the controller.
# It looks like a boot stall through every indirect signal (empty serial console, low CPU, MAC
# absent from the bridge) but the VM is up — it just has no network. Proven on the lab pool: adding
# exactly this file to the seed turned a "staller" into a VM that DHCPs and reports traffic.
#
# A clone of the golden image already carries golden's persisted network config on disk, so it does
# not strictly need this. Shipping it in every seed is still correct: a DHCP-on-ethernet config is
# what both paths want, and it makes the seed a complete datasource for the from-scratch import path
# as well as the clone path.
#
# `match: name: "e*"` covers both the classic `eth0` and predictable `en*` names without pinning one.
# It is static, nothing per-agent here, so when the plugin wires up the seed at M3 it attaches this
# file verbatim while user-data and meta-data carry rendered placeholders. Not wired up yet:
# provision() is inert today, same as user-data.tmpl.
#
---
version: 2
ethernets:
  primary:
    match:
      name: "e*"
    dhcp4: true
